-- pending: SPEC §21 Open (a div computation, a nested run_until_empty, inside a task of spawn)
-- now: 30:16: this argument of `push` has type `i32 * (mu X. 1 + ((mu X1. 1 + i32 * X1) + box top U (nu X. F ((mu X. 1 + i32 * X) + box top U X) & F 1)) * X)`, which is not `array A * i32`
-- A task that fans out: a request handler task spawns one subtask per backend it queries and
-- runs them to completion with a scheduler of its own, then combines their answers. The outer
-- scheduler runs two such handlers.
--
-- Exercises: `run_until_empty` inside a task (a scheduler nested in a task), `spawn` inside a
-- task, generic lists of lists.
--
-- Blocked by: a task whose body runs a loop that is not counted. `run_until_empty`'s rounds are
-- unbounded, so it is div, and `spawn` cannot wrap a div computation (SPEC §21 *Open*: no handler
-- wraps a div computation). The message is "this argument of `push` has type `i32 * (…)`, which
-- is not `array A * i32`": `push` falls back to `lib/buf.bc`'s.
--
-- Once it lands: `[[10, 11], [20, 21]]`.

include async

fn backend(n: i32) -> i32 with Async = await(); n

fn handle(base: i32) -> List[i32] with Async =
  await();
  let q = queue[i32]();
  let q = push(q, with spawn { backend(base) });
  let q = push(q, with spawn { backend(base + 1) });
  run_until_empty(q)

main -> List[List[i32]] =
  let q = queue[List[i32]]();
  let q = push(q, with spawn { handle(10) });
  let q = push(q, with spawn { handle(20) });
  run_until_empty(q)
